WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.827
Resample is designed for data that has a time component.

00:00:03.827 --> 00:00:12.442
Instead of grouping by a regular category such as region or channel, resample groups observations into time intervals.

00:00:12.442 --> 00:00:18.142
Those intervals might be days, weeks, months, quarters, or years.

00:00:18.142 --> 00:00:24.895
In the example, we convert the date column to datetime and then calculate daily sales totals.

00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:29.867
This pattern becomes very useful with transactional datasets.

00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:34.202
Imagine a table with hundreds of thousands of purchases.

00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:41.377
Looking at every transaction individually may not reveal a trend, but summarizing the data by week or month can make the

00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:44.297
pattern much easier to see.

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:47.592
Run the code using the daily frequency.

00:00:47.592 --> 00:00:52.892
Then change the frequency from D to W and compare the result.

00:00:52.892 --> 00:00:58.237
The important concept is that resample changes the level of time detail.

00:00:58.237 --> 00:01:02.902
We are moving from individual observations to regular time-based summaries.
